ripple-manifest.json: @ripple-ui/svelte 0.8.0 manifest, vendored from qbtrix/ripple-iui#185
(branch feat/illustration, which carries #182's data widgets plus illustration,
bill-split and the button's choice-card icon and description) at
ffed5443f5903f14410403dd7a1c9e9af6e033ad, pending a release.
It is that commit's packages/svelte/static/manifest.json (generatedAt
2026-10-09T18:15:59.014Z, 199 widgets, upstream sha256
4d9cc2cc15102be50c5d94e9a9c4a702570298b954a7924effb210961e3518ec), with every
widget's "example" removed. The server never reads the examples, and one carries a
sample Stripe-style key that GitHub push protection refuses.

Refresh (once the data widgets ship in a release, use the release asset):
  gh release download -R qbtrix/ripple-iui --pattern manifest.json -D <dir>
  (until then: packages/svelte/static/manifest.json at the PR head, after
  `bun run build:manifest` if it is stale)
  python -I - <dir>/manifest.json ee/pocketpaw_ee/paw_bar/ripple-manifest.json <<'PY'
  import json, sys
  m = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8"))
  for w in m["widgets"]:
      w.pop("example", None)
  open(sys.argv[2], "w", encoding="utf-8").write(json.dumps(m, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
  PY
then update this file and the pins in test_the_vendored_ripple_manifest_has_not_drifted
(tests/cloud/test_paw_bar_ripple_profile.py: _RIPPLE_MANIFEST_SHA256, version, count).
